ng connectivity given the unshown tile distribution.\\n\\nReason: W5 is the most isolated tile in my hand, sitting between two pairs (W3 and W6) but not contributing to any immediate meld formation. With only 3 W5 tiles unshown and my hand already having an exposed meld limiting high-scoring potential, keeping pairs (W3, W6, T4) and tiles near my existing Chow (B2, B4, B5) offers better flexibility for completing a basic winning hand quickly.\\n\\nAnswer: Play W5\"}"}
