nd **B4** are remnants from the exposed Chow, keeping them serves no purpose\n\nBetween W9, B2, and B4, **W9** is the safest discard as it's a terminal tile with poor connectivity.\n\nReason: \nW9 is an isolated terminal tile with very limited potential to form melds. With only W7(1) and W8(2) unshown, the chance of completing W7-W8-W9 is low. My pairs (W3, W6, T4) and potential sequences (T3-T4-T5) have better development potential. Discarding W9 maintains maximum flexibility for future draws.\n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
